  "description": "Decision 137: demand by distance and the outside connections, in a world 524288 x 196608 units (8.2 x 3.1 km). A stands at (100352, 100352), B 400 m east of it, D 1.75 km and C 3 km, on the line A-B-D-C; A starts 1000 trips a day and B, C and D draw 1000 each. Off, A's 1000 are shared equally by B, C and D: 334, 333, 333. With demand by distance each pair keeps a share of its trips by its straight-line distance, a tenth up to 500 m, all from 2 km and in a straight line between: 334 x 100 = 33, 333 x 1000 = 333, 333 x 850 = 283 (thousandths, rounded half up). Then the company is managed and the land, homes of 1000 residents on A's cell (row 24, column 24), sets the ridership: A and B share the cell by nearness (1000 : 750), 571 and 429 residents, 228 and 172 trips; C and D reach no land and have none. E stands 20000 units (312 m) inside the east edge, on the line Out from A. Without the outside connections it has no ridership and A sends B its 228, of which 400 m keep 23. With them E is an outside connection: the outside's 6000 trips a day are all its, A's 228 go 6 to B (kept 1) and 222 to E, all kept, and E's 6000 all go to A, the one station it reaches with ridership. A trip to or from E pays the standard 500 and the city's baseline of 75 more: 575.",
